<Project>

  <!-- Inherit the repository's settings rather than replacing them: a Directory.Build.props in a
       subdirectory shadows the one above it, so without this import the test projects would lose
       the target framework, the analyzer policy and warnings-as-errors all at once. -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Warnings stay errors here. These four rules are relaxed for test code only, each because it
         argues against something the suite does on purpose. Every exception is in this file with its
         reason, and there are no pragmas in test source.

         CA1707 - underscores in member names. A test name here is a sentence stating what must be
                  true: `A_malformed_id_does_not_parse`. The failure output is the sentence, which is
                  the whole point, and PascalCase would make every name less readable than the
                  assertion it introduces.
         CA1515 - types could be internal. MSTest discovers public test classes; making them internal
                  to satisfy a rule aimed at application assemblies would be tail-wagging.
         CA1307 - StringComparison on a comparison. Correct for production string handling and noise
                  inside an assertion, where the comparison is ordinal by inspection and a failing
                  test is read rather than relied upon by a caller.
         CA2007 - ConfigureAwait on an await. There is no synchronization context to capture in a
                  test host, so the call conveys nothing.
         CA1861 - a constant array argument hoisted to a static readonly field. The rule targets a
                  hot path called repeatedly; a test method runs once per case, and the array is the
                  expectation, which belongs beside the assertion that reads it rather than at the
                  top of the file away from the thing it describes. -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1707;CA1515;CA1307;CA2007;CA1861</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
